ARCUIA Sensor Fusion — Teensy setup 
Ryan Breen

see the root README for the project overview, numbers, and how the filter works. this file is just wiring + how to run the teensy code.

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ HARDWARE — SENSOR WIRING (Teensy 4.x) ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

IMU SDA / SCL → Teensy I2C pins (18 / 19) Or SPI: CS, MOSI, MISO, SCK → Teensy SPI0 (10-13) Outputs: accel [m/s²], gyro [rad/s] @ 500 Hz

Magnetometer SDA / SCL → same I2C bus as IMU (or second bus) Output: mag [µT] @ up to 500 Hz (can repeat last reading)

GPS / GNSS TX → Teensy Serial1 RX (pin 0) Configure module for 10 Hz updates, 115200 baud Parse: latitude [deg], longitude [deg], altitude [m], velocity NED [m/s]

Barometer Baro is computed from the ICAO standard atmosphere model using filtered altitude — no separate sensor needed unless you want to fuse raw pressure for altitude correction.

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ HOW TO RUN ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Open project in VS Code with PlatformIO installed
platformio.ini: [env:teensy41] platform = teensy board = teensy41 framework = arduino
In main.cpp:
Create AHRSFilter filter;
Call filter.update(accel, gyro, mag, 0.002f) in a 500 Hz ISR or timer
Call filter.feedGPS(lla, velNED) in your GPS parse callback
Call filter.printCSV() to stream data over USB Serial
Read the stream with visualize_live.py (see root README)